{"id":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"Agents","desc":"Who can be dispatched, one node per agent.\n\n**The roster (ruled by the human 2026-08-24 ~16:42, opencode removed ~16:45): THREE implementors — claude-opus, grok, pi. Reviewers: grok, pi (each reviews the others' work; an author never reviews its own lane). claude-fable reserved for design-grade work.**\n\n**Choosing an implementor when the human didn't specify (ruled ~17:05):** claude-opus for maximum intelligence on complex work — the default for anything design-heavy, cross-cutting, or subtle. Then grok — proven on infra-shaped and test-shaped work. pi is EXPERIMENTAL: it could be Opus-level or Grok-level, remains to be seen — its authoring outcomes (web-testlib-face, debate3-claim-tests, first PRs 2026-08-24) are the evidence being gathered; record wins and losses on its node.\n\n- **Launch command:** the `command` property is THE EXACT LAUNCH COMMAND — a launcher reads it and runs it verbatim.\n  - A missing node, or a node without `command`, REFUSES the spawn loudly; nobody falls back to a machine default.\n  - Reason: the Fable burn, 2026-08-13, is why this file exists.\n- **Role:** `role` says what the agent is for (`author`, `reviewer`, or `author+reviewer`).\n- **Split:** the note keeps the story and the quirks; the properties keep the facts.\n- **Spawn shape:** `kolu create --repo <repo> --worktree <branch> --json -- <command>`\n- When kolu grows a structured launch spec, these properties migrate into it.","changed":"2026-08-24T17:02:59-04:00","custom":{"merge-gate":"RULED by the human 2026-08-23 12:18, after the orchestrator merged #352 on a misread approval: NO PR IS MERGED WITHOUT THE HUMAN'S EXPLICIT APPROVAL OF THAT PR, given after its pipeline is complete (reviews folded, CI green, evidence verified) and the finished PR has been fielded to them. 'Auto-merge on verification' dispositions are void from now; 'approve' said mid-pipeline is not a merge gate. The orchestrator fields, the human merges — or says 'merge'."}}
{"id":"agent-claude-opus","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"claude-opus — the author agent","desc":"Claude Code pinned to Opus with the 1M context window (`opus[1m]`), YOLO mode. The default author for dispatched lanes. Verify with the banner: it must say Opus, not the machine default. The `[1m]` suffix is the human's ruling of 2026-08-21 — a lane that runs for hours must not compact itself into amnesia.","changed":"2026-08-21T21:52:55-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model opus[1m] --dangerously-skip-permissions","context":"1M — the [1m] suffix, ruled by the human 2026-08-21 (on the Anthropic API Opus 5 is 1M natively; the suffix pins it everywhere and is harmless where it is the default)","role":"author"}}
{"id":"agent-grok","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a1","title":"grok — author and reviewer","desc":"Grok CLI in always-approve mode.\n\n- Reviews in a split terminal of the author's worktree.\n- Posts one review comment via gh.\n- Never edits, pushes, or merges.\n- **TUI quirk (the human, 2026-08-24): a message sent while Grok is mid-turn is QUEUED by default — press Enter ONCE MORE to send it right away.** For the orchestrator's three-step submit against a busy grok: text → settle → Enter → (if the screen shows the message queued rather than steering) a second Enter.\n- **Authoring track record:**\n  - Shipped #64 (home-manager module) and #153 (parallel e2e) as author; the weekend flake campaign (#359/#360/#361/#363/#364) and #368's pin as author, all clean.\n  - 2026-08-16: its quiet-outline UI authoring attempt was judged bad by the human and discarded wholesale (terminal killed, no commits worth keeping).\n  - **Guidance:** prefer Opus for UI/design-heavy authoring, grok for reviews and infra/test-shaped authoring.","changed":"2026-08-24T17:07:11-04:00","custom":{"command":"grok --always-approve","role":"author+reviewer","usage-limit":"2026-08-22 09:40 — the status bar showed 'Weekly limit left: 8%'; the human: 'Don't worry about Grok; I can increase limit' — do NOT re-dispatch grok lanes on a low-limit reading; if a grok session actually dies on the limit, tell the human and wait"}}
{"id":"agent-claude-fable","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a3","title":"claude-fable — design-grade author","desc":"Claude Code pinned to Fable (the Mythos-tier model above Opus), YOLO mode. Added 2026-08-19 on the human's word, for design-first work (first use: the vault-in-browser design doc).\n- Reserve for work needing that level — it is the expensive tier; Opus stays the default author.\n- Verify with the banner: it must say Fable, not the machine default.","created":"2026-08-19T20:04:37-04:00","custom":{"command":"claude --model fable --dangerously-skip-permissions","role":"author"}}
{"id":"supervision-watcher","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a4","title":"Supervision: the watcher and the mute list","desc":"The wake mechanism (per instructions.md): `kolu watch --states waiting,awaiting --held-for 60s --nag 10m --ignore-self --heartbeat 30m` run under the harness's Monitor tool with `persistent: true` (a background Bash task notifies only on exit — a watch stream never exits; RCA 2026-08-21).\n\nThe mute list, as `--ignore` flags — fail-open (a stale id costs nothing; every NEW terminal still rings), which is what keeps it legal under the never-an-id-list doctrine. Muted 2026-08-21, all explicitly dispositioned as the HUMAN's own sessions: 0cdc41be + a5e17829 + ab047416 (the kolu#2194 handover — the human took that lane over with their own Claude; orchestrator stands down until handed back), aa15d349 (kolu·damn-spring), 3d01a0b3 (merged docs-PR session), 7251ff2b (nixos-config), 1ef72cfc (olai·master chat session), 2080355a. A terminal handed back to the orchestrator is unmuted by re-arming without its flag; a new human session that starts nagging gets muted the same way after its disposition is verified — never on assumption (identify via kolu ls first).\n\nNag discipline (RCA-2, 2026-08-21): a nag on an unchanged block is re-DERIVED, not re-acknowledged — the second nag with no new information means the block is suspect: act on standing authority or escalate it as a standalone question. A dismissal applies to an event, never to a terminal.","created":"2026-08-21T17:30:28-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T17:03:56-04:00","custom":{"deploy-2026-08-21":"DEPLOYED ~21:20 and then the orchestrator's own process restarted ~21:25 — the watch died loudly both times as designed and was re-armed (bhb2ugljn); the SECOND restart recycled all terminal ids (the kolu skill's warning made real): the A/B experiment terminal died, every lane's terminal prop went stale, the mute list was rewritten. Production kolu now carries #2194; full real-agent verification run 21:28 (test terminal c01109d6).","kolu-ci-fleet-2026-08-22":"ABANDONED 10:41 — Incus unstable: boxes created Ready at 10:00-10:03 were gone from `pu list` (ERR instance not found) within ~30 min, ci-2 mid-e2e; kolu-ci-8 created 10:38 by me (on linux-08) and left unused; kolu-ci-3 (linux-14) still alive but out of use by ruling","kolu-ci-fleet-gist":"https://gist.github.com/srid/143288f346ba71e27cfb54e67173e3b0 — the pu create failures of 2026-08-22 in full (timeline, outputs, raw server transcripts, registry state, questions for the pu owner)","kolu-pr-process":"RULED by the human 2026-08-22 16:15: kolu PRs are taken through KOLU's own process — the author runs kolu's /be skill (.agents/skills/be/SKILL.md in the kolu checkout) instead of our review/refactor round, and CI through kolu's /ci skill (.agents/skills/ci/SKILL.md) instead of our odu recipe; both platforms green before merge; the orchestrator merges on /be done + /ci green. 16:20: the darwin host /ci names (sincereintent) has been REPLACED by ci@petit (--host aarch64-darwin=ci@petit, under /tmp/olai-odu-petit.lock). Olai PRs keep our process. First applied to lane-scli PR 1 (surface-cli-kolu).","mute-list":"CORRECTED 2026-08-24 ~17:10 (the human): 🏠 d7543299 is THE ORCHESTRATOR ITSELF — this olai ACP chat session, whose headless claude-code the padi sees as a terminal. Muted as SELF (the --ignore-self case, hand-spelled because the orchestrator runs behind the chat panel, not inside a kolu terminal), never as the human's. 🔥 30f81ddc is the human's Fable agent on kolu (engageable on their word). Human's own: 724a754e (nixos-config grok) + splits; and the generalized rule — any terminal no lane's terminal prop names, outside olai's worktrees, is presumed the human's. A terminal INSIDE olai's worktrees that the orchestrator did not create (e.g. 52e990d4 ux-review-pi) is the human's spawn until handed over. Ids rotate on kaval restart — re-identify by intent/cwd","odu-venue":"RULING 10:50 2026-08-22 (human): kolu-ci-* dead. TWO venues in parallel, each one-run-at-a-time under a local flock: localhost x86_64-linux (/tmp/olai-odu-localhost.lock, --host x86_64-linux=localhost) and ci@petit aarch64-darwin (/tmp/olai-odu-petit.lock, --host aarch64-darwin=ci@petit) — the --host pin is mandatory (bare --platform dials dead kolu-ci boxes from hosts.json). For olai PRs EITHER platform green is the bar; kolu PRs need both. RULED 12:03 (human): olai's GitHub ruleset still requires the nine @x86_64-linux contexts — ADMIN MERGES ARE FINE for a macOS-only-green olai PR (`gh pr merge --squash --admin`); the ruleset is not narrowed. Measurements under the localhost flock. Brief: briefs/ci-venue-change.md.","odu-venue-update":"RULED by the human 2026-08-24 ~15:56: kolu-ci-* are back AND CAN BE USED — supersedes the 13:45 localhost-only ruling. The mandatory --host x86_64-linux=localhost pin (imposed 2026-08-22 10:50 because bare --platform dialed then-dead kolu-ci boxes) is lifted: CI may dial kolu-ci-* via odu's ordinary --platform path, with localhost (under its flock) and ci@petit (darwin, under its flock) still available. Either platform green remains the bar for olai PRs. In-flight briefs written under the old ruling stand unless re-instructed","verification-2026-08-21":"production kolu#2194 FULL TEST with a real agent (c01109d6, 21:28–21:35) — ALL STAGES PASSED: spawn+boot; typed prompt + Enter; READY 42 in 1s; settle → test watch (--held-for 10s) transition at +10s arriving instantly (per-line flush VERIFIED); nag re-ring at exactly +45s and +90s; main watch (--held-for 60s) transition at +60s; second prompt → second transition; screen_text, kolu ls, --ignore mute list, --ignore-self, --heartbeat; loud death + re-arm twice; kill → terminal gone, state-knob watch silent by design (no gone event, per the contract). Orchestrator's verdict on #2194: GOOD — every claim exercised live on the production build; merge-ready from the consumer's seat.","watch-task":"RE-ARMED 2026-08-24 ~15:35 on the human's word after the orchestrator's process restart killed bowney4oj (which itself replaced b5o3nevw7 and bn865br9z across earlier restarts): Monitor task bmsrte0cx, kolu watch --states waiting,awaiting --held-for 60s --nag 10m, persistent, fleet-wide. Zero orchestrator lanes live at arming — the watch stands ready for the next dispatch. Find this node by prop:mute-list"}}
{"id":"agent-pi","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a2V","title":"pi — author AND reviewer (kimi-k3 by default)","desc":"The pi CLI on its default model (kimi-k3). Added 2026-08-24 on the human's word: BOTH an implementor and a reviewer — the third author beside claude-opus and grok.\n\n- **Track record:** reviewed #366 (DO-NOT-OBJECT with the shippable-without-guard counter-argument the human arbitrated — a real position, well argued), #367 (found the REAL maxBuffer-contract inversion as its MUST, mechanically probed) and #368 (OBJECT with 2 legitimate MUSTs). **Authoring: TWO wins on day one, 2026-08-24** — debate3-claim-tests (#370, merged de40d859: mutation-verified sweeps, 0-MUST verdict, SHOULD folds beyond the ask) and web-testlib-face (#372, merged 42987d90: the 19-trespass door with closure-walk fence, fold work mutation-proven, disciplined flake attribution). Both rode the master-red repair cleanly. Early verdict: performing at the complex end — closer to Opus-shaped than Grok-shaped so far.\n- Boots to a plain composer fast; token counters in the status bar are the working signal (no Esc:cancel footer like grok).\n- Reviews in a split of the author's worktree, posts one comment via gh, never edits/pushes/merges — the standard reviewer contract.","created":"2026-08-24T16:40:49-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T18:06:28-04:00","custom":{"command":"pi","model":"kimi-k3 (pi's own default; no flag needed)","role":"author+reviewer"}}
